ink all of us have to say that's not  normal that's not okay and speak back to  it there's and isn't this book James  Comey your way of speaking out and  drawing attention to say to the people  that listen it's not normal what's  happening in the White House is not  normal and we've got to figure out a way  to stop this and correct it isn't that  what you're doing in part I mean I think  what I can do is make a small  contribution by asking  questions about what matters and what  unites us which is our values and we're  losing track of and becoming numb to the  erosion of our core values of truth than  the rule of law no but you say the  president is unethical untethered to the  truth institutional values his  leadership is transactional ego driven  and about personal loyalty and some  people are raising that those exact  things about you people can say whatever  they want Mike might what I hope people  will do is not get caught down in the  back-and-forth of Twitter personnel and  personal conflicts but ask themselves  what unites us in this country the truth  the rule of law equal protection of the  laws and it's not okay for the President  of the United States to attack those  things and to routinely lie no matter  what your politics it's just not okay  aside from the President of the United  States you also said that you lost trust  and leadership at the DOJ starting with  Jeff Sessions and in broad Rosenstein  I'm curious as to whether any of that  trust has come back given some of their  actions as of late rod Rosen side said  the DOJ won't be extorted Jeff Sessions  reportedly said that he would be that he  would resign if rod Rosen Stein was  fired do you find that reassuring I do  I was critical of them when I thought  they were acting in a way that was not  consistent with the values of the  department I think since then especially  the Deputy Attorney General has acted  consistent with those values and  protected the rule of law can I pull us  away from a