ion where I  didn't anticipate how people might hear  my words differently than I intended  them if you were interviewing the  president what would you ask him well  I'd ask him if I were Bob Muller I'd ask  him a whole lot of questions and I would  want as much time as I needed to be able  to conduct a competent investigation  interview how much time would that it  would all depend upon how  straightforward the witness was and  whether the witness answer the questions  questions like what because we know  you'd ask a lot of questions you can  hear your top two questions that you  want to know well you certainly looking  at the question of obstruction of  justice we want to understand what his  State of Mind was around things like his  conversation with me on Valentine's Day  I have one view of that but I don't know  what was in his head and that's critical  to the question of obstruction so you'd  want to know what were you thinking and  why do you say that and who did you talk  to about that tell me why that helps  because if you were asking me that  question I would say well I do I wasn't  trying to obstruct anything Rudy  Giuliani he said you wouldn't tell the  president he was in the clear and that  that was grounds enough for him to fire  you since he's essentially your boss  well you'd want to ask follow-up  questions based on the other  investigation that you've done the  reason you interview a subject towards  the end of the investigation as we did  with Hillary Clinton is you've gathered  all kinds of facts documents other  people's recollections that you can use  to test what that subject says to you  one of the things really Giuliani says  is you told her Laurie Clinton she was  in the clear why couldn't you have said  that publicly about President Trump we  completed the investigation of Secretary  Clinton and announced its completion  there's an ongoing investigation near as  I can tell and I don't know how the  special counsel will approach it but  they're two very different things next  week though rather will be a year since  the firing we all remember watching it  on TV it was painful to watch and it was  a painful day for you and in this in  that past year you've had time to  reflect what are you thinking now James  Comey about how you've handled yourself  in the last year what you see  for yourself going forward where are you  now I am looking backwards proud of the  work that the FBI has done we really did  act consistent with our values have a  great sense of pain over a lot that's  going on especially our being stuck in  the middle of the election but I'm at  peace with the decisions we made I keep  saying we because I'm accountable for  the decisions but it was a large group  of talented people who made those-- and  I'm a happy person despite a lot of the  rocks thrown and I'm gonna teach  starting in the fall which would be  really cool because young people talk  about holding you accountable  it'll be stimulating James come me thank  you so much for joining thanks really do  you I know we're your last TV interview  I'd like to think you saved the best for  last certainly do really good to meet  you thank you all and say hi to your  wife I will thank you a higher loyalty  is on sale now wherever you'd like to  buy your book

